{"authored" [{"question" "q-327669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=7 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=6\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={7}^{2}+(6\\sqrt{2})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =49+72 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =121 \\\\ R & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08bcaf2275f6a7d81618e8747f39d4bcf31b9158c54efcd1c55ad80ea1df2f7c" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327669" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0,$ what is the **exact** value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($ \n{{field-1}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08bcaf2275f6a7d81618e8747f39d4bcf31b9158c54efcd1c55ad80ea1df2f7c" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327979" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08bcaf2275f6a7d81618e8747f39d4bcf31b9158c54efcd1c55ad80ea1df2f7c" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference