 "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+1.351)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-107577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+1.107)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $R>0,$ what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for cosine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08bcaf2275f6a7d81618e8747f39d4bcf31b9158c54efcd1c55ad80ea1df2f7c" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274609" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274609" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {R}^{2} & =3 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08bcaf2275f6a7d81618e8747f39d4bcf31b9158c54efcd1c55ad80ea1df2f7c" 