e5c33a802e6b683b31f993bc8" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.054)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "18fc56496facbcd125d957c87864399173e648ee5c33a802e6b683b31f993bc8" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.854)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "18fc56496facbcd125d957c87864399173e648ee5c33a802e6b683b31f993bc8" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-327669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-327669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=7 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=6\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={7}^{2}+(6\\sqrt{2})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =49+72 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =121 \\\\ R & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-327669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cab1d110fad91a5454cc07913f68c920bed3a02a2543671beb0be3c79578ed7e"} {"question" "q-327669" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-327669" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-11296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-11296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =16+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-11296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cab1d110fad91a5454cc07913f68c920bed3a02a2543671beb0be3c79578ed7e"} {"question" "q-11296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-11296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-11296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-80127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-80127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/state.json" "file_sha256" "b268fa94565c1db9deea58ee11f8fdf2750b0acf594557f8dfa6a48f0b6a47b2"} {"question" "q-80127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038530/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cab1d110fad91a5